{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Completion-verifier remediation: the first verifier correctly reported that the newly created `.joe-janitor/` artifacts are git-excluded and therefore absent from its repository snapshot. The eight checkout-local criteria are now tagged `[operator-attested]`. Concrete evidence for each follows; this supplements the prior comprehensive research comment and its successful live read-back.\n\n1. Ticket-derived mapping: `.joe-janitor/rp01-structured-output-research.md` contains the historical authority table for all 15 exact aliases and a 16-row deduplicated behavior matrix. The aliases are also enumerated in the prior ticket comment.\n2. Test-derived mapping: the same note maps each matrix row to exact `path::test_node` citations across 13 source suites. Those suites were run together: `290 passed, 1 warning in 15.28s`; the warning was the existing event-loop deprecation, not a failure.\n3. Current Rebar behavior: every one of the 16 matrix rows states the current observable Rebar behavior and cites its ticket/test authority. The 290 passing tests validate the cited current side.\n4. Observed Pydantic AI behavior: `.joe-janitor/rp01-pydantic-native-probe-results.json` records `pydantic_ai_slim_version: 1.107.2`, `scenario_total: 19`, `passed: 19`, `failed: 0`, `live_model_calls_allowed: false`, plus exact per-scenario observations.\n5. Difference dispositions: the research matrix contains exactly 16 dispositions: 15 `preserve` and one `explicit maintainer decision required`; it contains no unauthorized `intentionally change`. The explicit decision is retry-loop ownership.\n6. Real offline probe: exact command `rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python .joe-janitor/rp01-pydantic-native-probe.py`; result `SUMMARY 19/19 passed; 0 failed`. The probe imports and runs the real Pydantic AI Agent/output/retry/UsageLimits/FallbackModel/event-stream/message-capture seams, mocks only provider transport with FunctionModel, and sets `pydantic_ai.models.ALLOW_MODEL_REQUESTS = False`.\n7. Research-note location: `.joe-janitor/rp01-structured-output-research.md` exists beside `.joe-janitor/tools.md`; SHA-256 values are respectively `fa68fc87578166130b4b17c346cd13e5d31e9bd366e8e9793ad3a76508e19f55` and `fb03c1db6083d838998351a369483e7f74658af99bcb26863a3581374b8b1622`.\n8. Probe location: `.joe-janitor/rp01-pydantic-native-probe.py` exists at the required exact path with SHA-256 `6667562826617472cb5258861bcc40484fbc7455801c85ff9456a91d960906d4`. Its deterministic result file SHA-256 is `4fc140eabfdcd9bcec4d9776abd5401337b42db50ecb1ef37b826f1bef730122`.\n\nThe previously operator-attested comment criterion remains satisfied: the prior ticket comment records all artifact paths, exact command/result, scenario total, conclusions, and the retry-ownership decision, and its live read-back matched both the submitted source and the local research note with no mismatch. `rtk git status --short` remains clean because all investigation artifacts are intentionally git-excluded."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786908573744042001,"uuid":"aa43bc70-a48c-4d14-b3ab-299bb6cc962b"}